# W4-C (2026-11-13): scripts that run in a POSIX shell or a container build are LF in every checkout. Without these
# rules core.autocrlf=true checked them out CRLF ("set -eu\r" breaks sh, sh -n fails on load-images.sh), so an
# air-gapped bundle or an image built from a Windows checkout shipped broken scripts. The index already holds them as
# LF, so these rules change no committed bytes. Guard: test_workflow_guards.py LineEndings (governance.yml).
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.envsh         text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
mvnw            text eol=lf
entrypoint      text eol=lf
*-entrypoint    text eol=lf
# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF (cmd.exe needs it for labels and goto; Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads them as such).
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
# Binary: never converted, never diffed as text.
